                <pb facs="0411" n="287" sameAs="frus:frus1921v01/pg287"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">824.00/180: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Uruguay</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Jeffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Montevideo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1921-02-09T16:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 9,
                                1921—4 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 11:50
                    p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>6. Department’s 3, February 5th, 5 [<hi rendition="#italic">6</hi>] p.m. Foreign
                    Office informs me Uruguayan Government had already resolved to recognize present
                    Constitutional Government of Bolivia, and that it has instructed the Chargé
                    d’Affaires appointed to La Paz to proceed immediately to his post. On his
                    arrival notification of recognition will be extended through him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jeffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
